imgui.ini

# CTest run output (Testing/TAG, Testing/Temporary/, per-run XML). Generated by
# every `ctest` invocation; three of these files were tracked until 2026-08-07,
# and because the path was NOT ignored the tracked-and-ignored guard could not
# see them. Ignoring the directory is what makes that guard able to catch a
# recurrence.
Testing/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LARGE-ASSET GATE
#
# 556 MiB of the 582 MiB this repo tracks outside third_party/ sits in 37 files.
# AGENTS.md section "Large tracked assets" has the inventory and why those 37
# stay where they are: documented, not rewritten (owner decision 2026-09-15 - no
# filter-repo, no BFG, no LFS). The rules below are the other half of that
# decision - they stop NEW heavy binaries from joining them.
#
# These rules are safe to add to a repo that already tracks such files: git
# never applies an ignore rule to a path that is already in the index. Each rule
# below that could match a tracked file names it back with a `!` line anyway, so
# the tracked-and-ignored gate
# (scripts/windows/tests/Repo.GeneratedArtifacts.Tests.ps1) can keep asserting
# the general property instead of carrying exceptions.
#
# Adding one on purpose is still possible and still deliberate:
#   git add -f <path>
# then add a `!` line here and a line to the AGENTS.md inventory. The friction
# is the feature - a 90 MiB mesh is a decision, not a `git add .`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# DCC project files. Editable source art runs 10-100x the size of the mesh
# exported from it and nothing in this tree reads it. One is tracked
# (New_0.9.blend, 66 MiB); it is the ceiling, not the precedent.
*.blend
!Resources/Models/Sulo/New_0.9.blend
*.fbx
*.max
*.ma
*.mb
*.c4d
*.3ds
*.ztl
*.spp
*.psd
*.xcf

# Archives and disk images. A repo that needs one has a packaging step; a
# committed blob is a packaging step nobody can re-run.
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz
*.iso

# Video. Screenshots under images/ are PNG and stay. A capture belongs in a
# release asset or on the homepage, not in the clone every contributor pays for.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
*.mkv
*.webm

# Heavy image formats under Resources/. Scoped rather than repo-wide on purpose:
# the vendored third_party/KTX test corpus is tracked directly here and owns its
# own .exr/.hdr/.dds/.tga files. Runtime textures are PNG/JPG and unaffected.
Resources/**/*.tif
Resources/**/*.tiff
Resources/**/*.exr
Resources/**/*.hdr
Resources/**/*.tga
Resources/**/*.dds
!Resources/Models/Sulo/WolfStahl/textures/MetalSpottyDiscoloration001_DISP16_4K_METALNESS.tif

# Wavefront meshes: 33 files, 402 MiB, 69% of everything this repo tracks. The
# 33 are listed back so a 34th has to be typed rather than swept in. (Compiler
# .obj output never reaches here - it lands under the build*/ directories
# ignored above, which is why the `# *.obj` line in the Compiled Object files
# block is commented out.)
Resources/**/*.obj
